# Shell scripts must be checked out with LF endings.
#
# This is not cosmetic. These scripts are copied to Linux hosts and run there,
# and a CRLF copy dies on the first line with "set: pipefail: 无效的选项名"
# before executing anything. Under cron that failure is silent: the job simply
# does not do its work and nothing reports it. The repository is edited on
# Windows, where core.autocrlf rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout, so the
# endings need to be pinned here rather than left to the local git config.
*.sh text eol=lf
